# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile does two bad things.
#
# It overwrites the linux node_modules that `COPY --from=deps` just installed
# with whatever is on the build machine. On Windows that means
# node_modules/@img/sharp-win32-x64 lands in a linux/amd64 image and sharp
# throws on the first photo resize. CI never sees it, because actions/checkout
# produces no node_modules at all — so the bug is invisible until the first
# local build, and then it is invisible again because it only fires at runtime.
#
# And it drags .env.local into the build context. That file holds live
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY and STRIPE_SECRET_KEY. Anything in the
# build context is readable from the image layers by anyone who can pull it.
.git
.github
.vercel
.claude
node_modules
.next
dist
mobile
photos
docs
